  {
   "id": "f760Lo2tBgAJ",
   "from": "ken.k...@gmail.com",
   "author": "4f80e1927b0757cb",
   "date": "2019-02-25T15:26:41Z",
   "subject": "Re: csvToUMF",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Tam,<div><br></div><div>csvToUMF requires very specific column names to work (which is a little unclear in the documentation). If you rename your obs.1-obs.27 columns to y.1-y.27 instead and rename &quot;location&quot; to &quot;site&quot;, it should import correctly:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">unmarked</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stringr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>inp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;trialds2.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> str_replace</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;obs&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;y&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;site&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>write</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">file</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;trialds2_new.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>test </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> csvToUMF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;trialds2_new.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;unmarkedFrameOccu&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>Ken</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Monday, February 25, 2019 at 5:06:53 AM UTC-5, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tamari...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I have the same issue and i tried to change the label with a separator but it still gives me error:(</div><div><div>Error in validObject(.Object) : </div><div>  invalid class “unmarkedFrame” object: obsCovData does not have M*obsNum rows.</div><div><br></div><div>I dont really understand what does this time says and I have attached the csv file, i wonder if i made any other mistake as well.</div><br>Thanks!! Look forward to your help:)</div><div><br></div><div>Best, </div><div>Tam<br><br><br><br>On Friday, February 27, 2015 at 7:47:30 AM UTC+8, Dan Linden wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Brian, make sure your observation-level columns are labeled with a separator between the name and number:<br><br>y.1 y.2 y.3<br>date.1 date.2 date.3<br><br>If you do this, your original csvToUMF call should work.<br></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
